title USB enumeration and driver binding

participant "bus / device" as device
participant "HCD (xhci/dwc3)" as HCD
participant "usbcore / hub thread" as usbcore
participant "driver (usbhid)" as driver

note right of driver: driver register interface

note over usbcore,driver: Driver registered earlier (module load)
driver->driver:prepare id_table
driver->usbcore: **usb_register(&usb_driver)**
note over usbcore,driver: usbcore keeps driver's **id_table** + probe()

note left of device: device plugged in
device->HCD: port status change
HCD->usbcore: hub interrupt URB

usbcore->device: **SET_ADDRESS**

usbcore->device: GET_DESCRIPTOR(**DEVICE**)
device-->usbcore: VID/PID, class, #config

usbcore->device: GET_DESCRIPTOR(**CONFIG**)
device-->usbcore: config + interfaces + endpoints

usbcore->usbcore: usb_parse_configuration()
usbcore->usbcore: usb_choose_configuration()

note left of device: device configured
usbcore->device: **SET_CONFIGURATION**

usbcore->usbcore: one struct usb_interface per interface
usbcore->usbcore: device_add(&intf->dev) -> driver core

note over usbcore: Match: interface descriptor <-> **id_table**\n- class/subclass/protocol\n- VID/PID
usbcore->driver: match found -> **probe(intf)**
note over usbcore,driver: If driver not registered yet: uevent (MODALIAS)\n-> modprobe -> usb_register() -> match again

driver->HCD: **usb_submit_urb(urb_irq)** IN
note over driver,HCD: URB queued, HCD polls the endpoint every bInterval

note left of device: Host polling data
loop every bInterval
    HCD->device: IN token
    alt no data
        device-->HCD: NAK
    else data ready
        device-->HCD: data
        HCD->driver: URB complete callback
        driver->driver: process data
        driver->HCD: usb_submit_urb() again
    end
end